    "body": "## Research done - broken down into sub-issues\n\n**Open questions answered**\n1. *Representation* - public literature (Stifter 1995 dexel critique; Inui et al. triple-dexel; Museth 2013 / OpenVDB) agrees that re-sampling a dexel or tri-dexel/voxel model onto a new axis-aligned grid after a flip loses accuracy at the grid pitch; tri-dexel is less biased but not rotation-invariant. Decision: keep **one canonical workpiece in the part frame** (the existing field/SDF engine, with dual contouring #23 for display/export) and evaluate it through each setup's transform; re-sample only where a grid must be axis-aligned, stating the pitch; Solidcore (#27) B-rep remains the exact long-term route.\n2. *Transform* - a rigid transform stored on the setup, from the work offset placement/orientation (#196, 3-2-1 #187), re-clamp presets, or a datum transfer.\n3. *Laws* - CLIP / named refusal stay as the fallback where the carried body cannot be judged; upstream digests + the transform enter later setups' stamps (Stale on change).\n4. *Rest* - `rest::prior_*` / `ahead_of` read the carried body; consumers: adaptive, pocket, 3D rough, rest machining, facing.\n5-8. *Lathe second op, fixtures, UI, performance* - one combined sub-issue (lathe/fixture/cache) plus a UI sub-issue; the stock source is a user parameter with a default.\n9. *Prior art (behaviour only, public docs)*: CAM systems present this as \"stock from preceding setup\" + \"continue rest machining\", and warn that displayed in-process stock goes stale until the earlier setup is re-simulated. A machine's G54 is translation only; a rotated part frame is either baked into the coordinates by the post or done by a control cycle (G68/G68.2, CYCLE800).\n\n**Work-offset issues (WCS) covered**\n- #315 **P0** - a rotated work offset (3-2-1 / `SetWcsOrigin` rotation) posts unrotated coordinates: the post only subtracts `OriginX/Y/Z`. Refuse by name first, then support.\n- #196 **P1** (existing) - per-setup work offset; the slot is currently inferred per operation from its height references (`posting::wcs_context`). Prerequisite of #316.\n\n**Sub-issues**\n| # | Priority | What |\n|---|---|---|\n| #315 | P0 | rotated work offset posts unrotated coordinates |\n| #196 | P1 | work offset per setup (existing) |\n| #316 | P1 | rigid setup-to-setup transform (presets, from offset/datum) |\n| #317 | P1 | program sim carries the machined body into the next setup |\n| #318 | P1 | rest across setups + Stale propagation |\n| #319 | P1 | generation and verification in later setups use the carried body |\n| #320 | P2 | Setup page: stock source parameter + incoming-stock display (needs #45) |\n| #321 | P2 | fixture collision, lathe second op, caching |\n\nOrder: #315 -> #196 -> #316 -> #317 -> #318 -> #319, then #320 / #321.\n\nPer AGENTS.md (\"needs-research is research, not code\"): every sub-issue is filed and linked, so `needs-research` is dropped and this umbrella closes; the work continues in the sub-issues.\n",
    "author_association": "OWNER",
